    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "#Create Your Credibility & Trust Meter\r\nCreate a tool that helps you decide: Does this actually hold up or does it just feel convincing?\r\n\r\n##Step 1: \r\n\r\n- Create a 5-level Credibility & Trust Meter that ranges from: **Highly Trustworthy → Falls Apart**\r\n\r\n##Step 2: Define It\r\n\r\n- For each of the 5 levels, write:\r\n\t- What makes something land here?\r\n\t- What kind of evidence is present?\r\n\t- What is missing (if anything)?\r\n\t- What would move it down one level?\r\n\r\n**Be specific. Avoid vague labels like “good” or “bad.”**\r\n\r\n##Step 3: Make It Usable\r\n\r\n- Under your meter, add 2–3 Stress Test Questions you can use anytime, such as:\r\n\t- What proof is given?\r\n\t- What details are missing?\r\n\t- What assumptions are being made?\r\n\t- Would this hold up in real life?"
  },
